            "marks": [
             {
              "type": "bold"
             }
            ],
            "text": "Eti"
           },
           {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ": HTN (USU bilat in adults) · older pts · nasal neoplasms "
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "attrs": {
           "indLeft": 0,
           "indRight": 0,
           "indFirst": 0,
           "spaceBefore": 0,
           "spaceAfter": 1.35,
           "line": null,
           "align": "left",
           "shade": null,
           "borders": null,
           "marker": null
          },
          "content": [
           {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "•may cause "
           },
           {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
             {
              "type": "bold"
             },
             {
              "type": "color",
              "attrs": {
               "hex": "ED7D31"
              }
             }
            ],
            "text": "bleed in both nare & posterior pharynx"
           },
           {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
             {
              "type": "color",
              "attrs": {
               "hex": "ED7D31"
              }
             }
            ],
            "text": " "
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "attrs": {
           "indLeft": 0,
           "indRight": 0,
           "indFirst": 0,
           "spaceBefore": 0,
           "spaceAfter": 1.35,
           "line": null,
           "align": "left",
           "shade": null,
           "borders": null,
           "marker": null
          },
          "content": [
           {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "•Woodruff plexus = sphenopalatine + pharyngeal a. anastomoses - less common · USU sig trauma · heavier bleed (can be life-threatening) · more extensive mgnt"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "attrs": {
           "indLeft": 0,
           "indRight": 0,
           "indFirst": 0,
           "spaceBefore": 0,
           "spaceAfter": 1.35,
           "line": null,
           "align": "left",
           "shade": null,
           "borders": null,
           "marker": null
          },
          "content": [
           {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "ddx juvenile nasopharyngeal angiofibroma: highly vasc benign tumor - MC adolescent boys - triad nasal obstruct · epistaxis (severe · can be life-threatening) · nasal drainage - CT or MRI w contrast → nasopharyngeal mass w widening of pterygomaxillary fissure"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "attrs": {
           "indLeft": 0,
           "indRight": 0,
           "indFirst": 0,
           "spaceBefore": 0,
           "spaceAfter": 1.35,
           "line": null,
           "align": "left",
           "shade": null,
           "borders": null,
           "marker": null
          }
         },
         {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "attrs": {
           "indLeft": 0,
           "indRight": 0,
           "indFirst": 0,
           "spaceBefore": 0,
           "spaceAfter": 1.35,
           "line": null,
           "align": "left",
           "shade": null,
           "borders": null,
           "marker": null
          },
          "content": [
           {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
             {
              "type": "italic"
             },
             {
              "type": "shade",
              "attrs": {
               "hex": "F7CAAC"
              }
             }
            ],
            "text": "*recurr epistaxis requires r/o of HTN & hypercoag dx"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "attrs": {
           "indLeft": 0,
           "indRight": 0,
           "indFirst": 0,
           "spaceBefore": 0,
           "spaceAfter": 1.35,
           "line": null,
           "align": "left",
           "shade": null,
           "borders": null,
           "marker": null
          },
          "content": [
           {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Eval: children may need sedation or topical vasoconstrictor/anesthetic (lidocaine ± oxymetazoline) to inspect - anterior rhinoscopy or otoscope w lrg tip"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "attrs": {
           "indLeft": 0,
           "indRight": 0,
           "indFirst": 0,
           "spaceBefore": 0,
           "spaceAfter": 1.35,
           "line": null,
           "align": "left",
           "shade": null,
           "borders": null,
           "marker": null
          },
          "content": [
           {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Labs & hematologist consult: <2yo · recurr >2-3x/wk · prolonged despite adequate local P & acute measures"
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       },
