             },
             {
              "type": "color",
              "attrs": {
               "hex": "4472C4"
              }
             }
            ],
            "text": "direct P (compress nasal alae) x5-10min · seating · leaning forward"
           },
           {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
             {
              "type": "color",
              "attrs": {
               "hex": "4472C4"
              }
             }
            ],
            "text": " "
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "attrs": {
           "indLeft": 0,
           "indRight": 0,
           "indFirst": 0,
           "spaceBefore": 0,
           "spaceAfter": 1.35,
           "line": null,
           "align": "left",
           "shade": null,
           "borders": null,
           "marker": null
          },
          "content": [
           {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "•short-acting topical decongestants (Afrin (oxymetazoline) · phenylephrine · cocaine)"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "attrs": {
           "indLeft": 0,
           "indRight": 0,
           "indFirst": 0,
           "spaceBefore": 0,
           "spaceAfter": 1.35,
           "line": null,
           "align": "left",
           "shade": null,
           "borders": null,
           "marker": null
          },
          "content": [
           {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "•still bleeding → remove clots → topical vasoconstrictor (oxymetazoline) → cautery → nasal packing (placed by ENT)"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "attrs": {
           "indLeft": 0,
           "indRight": 0,
           "indFirst": 0,
           "spaceBefore": 0,
           "spaceAfter": 1.35,
           "line": null,
           "align": "left",
           "shade": null,
           "borders": null,
           "marker": null
          },
          "content": [
           {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "•vasoconstrictor (oxymetazoline or phenylephrine) injected into nostril or on cotton pledget → direct compress x5min - still bleeding → chem (silver nitrate) or electrical cautery"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "attrs": {
           "indLeft": 0,
           "indRight": 0,
           "indFirst": 0,
           "spaceBefore": 0,
           "spaceAfter": 1.35,
           "line": null,
           "align": "left",
           "shade": null,
           "borders": null,
           "marker": null
          },
          "content": [
           {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "•visualize septum · nasal cavity · inferior turbinates & nasopharynx for source - ⍉source found → sus posterior → ENT for packing or endoscopy"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "attrs": {
           "indLeft": 0,
           "indRight": 0,
           "indFirst": 0,
           "spaceBefore": 0,
           "spaceAfter": 1.35,
           "line": null,
           "align": "left",
           "shade": null,
           "borders": null,
           "marker": null
          },
          "content": [
           {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "•oxymetazoline preferred in children - ⍉phenylephrine <12yo (sig morbidity & mortality w topical use in children)"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "attrs": {
           "indLeft": 0,
           "indRight": 0,
           "indFirst": 0,
           "spaceBefore": 0,
           "spaceAfter": 1.35,
           "line": null,
           "align": "left",
           "shade": null,
           "borders": null,
           "marker": null
          },
          "content": [
           {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "•"
           },
           {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
             {
              "type": "bold"
             }
            ],
            "text": "nasal packing"
           },
           {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ": requires abx (cephalosporin) to prevent toxic shock syndrome"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "attrs": {
           "indLeft": 0,
           "indRight": 0,
           "indFirst": 0,
           "spaceBefore": 0,
           "spaceAfter": 1.35,
           "line": null,
           "align": "left",
           "shade": null,
           "borders": null,
           "marker": null
          },
          "content": [
           {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "•petroleum jelly or abx ointment inside nostril BID x4-5d - cauterization"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "attrs": {
           "indLeft": 0,
           "indRight": 0,
           "indFirst": 0,
           "spaceBefore": 0,
           "spaceAfter": 1.35,
           "line": null,
           "align": "left",
           "shade": null,
           "borders": null,
           "marker": null
          },
          "content": [
           {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "•chem cautery w silver nitrate (if vessel visualized)"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "attrs": {
           "indLeft": 0,
           "indRight": 0,
           "indFirst": 0,
           "spaceBefore": 0,
           "spaceAfter": 1.35,
           "line": null,
           "align": "left",
           "shade": null,
           "borders": null,
           "marker": null
          },
          "content": [
           {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "•silver nitrate stick to sm area around bleed site - ⍉intact skin · electrocautery often superior but USU requires gen anesthesia"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "attrs": {
           "indLeft": 0,
           "indRight": 0,
           "indFirst": 0,
           "spaceBefore": 0,
           "spaceAfter": 1.35,
           "line": null,
           "align": "left",
           "shade": null,
           "borders": null,
           "marker": null
          },
          "content": [
           {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "•prevent recurr: nasal humidification · ⍉local trauma - recurr + allergic rhinitis → d/c IN corticosteroids · switch to PO antihist"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "attrs": {
           "indLeft": 0,
           "indRight": 0,
           "indFirst": 0,
           "spaceBefore": 0,
           "spaceAfter": 1.35,
           "line": null,
           "align": "left",
           "shade": null,
           "borders": null,
           "marker": null
          },
          "content": [
           {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "•children: humidifier at night (or nasal saline) · discourage nose picking · trim fingernails"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "attrs": {
           "indLeft": 0,
           "indRight": 0,
           "indFirst": 0,
           "spaceBefore": 0,
           "spaceAfter": 1.35,
           "line": null,
           "align": "left",
           "shade": null,
           "borders": null,
           "marker": null
          },
          "content": [
           {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "•comp: septal necrosis (if both sides of septum cauterized) · toxic shock syndrome (prolonged packing → fever · hypotension · desquamation · mucosal hyperemia) · infect"
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "attrs": {
           "indLeft": 0,
           "indRight": 0,
           "indFirst": 0,
           "spaceBefore": 0,
           "spaceAfter": 1.35,
           "line": null,
